%I A332217 #20 Oct 04 2026 15:10:26
%S A332217 2,8,18,49,50,72,128,162,169,196,200,242,361,441,450,512,578,648,676,
%T A332217 784,961,968,1058,1152,1225,1250,1369,1444,1458,1521,1682,1764,1800,
%U A332217 1849,2178,2312,2704,3136,3200,3249,3362,3721,3844,3969,4050,4225,4232,4418,4489,4608,4802,4900,5000
%N A332217 Numbers k for which the 2-adic valuation of sigma(k) is zero and its 3-adic valuation is 1 (so that sigma(k) is an odd multiple of 3, but not of 9).
%C A332217 From _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026: (Start)
%C A332217 The sequence contains only squares and twice squares (A028982).
%C A332217 If the factor 3 in sigma arises from the power of 2 that divides k, then k is twice a square of the form 2^e * m^2, where e == 1 or 3 (mod 6), m is odd, and every prime p == 1 (mod 3) dividing m has valuation v_p(m) != 1 (mod 3).
%C A332217 If the factor 3 in sigma arises from a power of an odd prime that divides k, then k is a square of the form 2^e * m^2, where e >= 0 is even, m is odd and has exactly one prime factor p == 1 (mod 3) with valuation v_p(m) == 1 or 7 (mod 9). (End)
%H A332217 Antti Karttunen, <a href="/A332217/b332217.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..10000</a>
%H A332217 <a href="/index/Si#SIGMAN">Index entries for sequences related to sigma(n)</a>.
%F A332217 {k: A000035(A000203(k))*A007949(A000203(k))==1}.
%F A332217 Sum_{n>=1} 1/a(n) = zeta(2) * Product_{primes p == 1 (mod 3)} ((p^4+1)/(p^4+p^2+1)) + (10/21 + Sum_{primes p == 1 (mod 3)} (p^2*(p^12+1)/((p^4+1)*(p^12+p^6+1)))) = 0.810741302424... . - _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 02 2026
%t A332217 Select[Range[5*10^3], IntegerExponent[DivisorSigma[1, #], {2, 3}] === {0, 1} &] (* _Michael De Vlieger_, Feb 12 2020 *)
%o A332217 (PARI) isA332217(n) = ((sigma(n)%2)&&(valuation(sigma(n),3)==1));
%Y A332217 Subsequence of A067051, which is a subsequence of A028982.
%Y A332217 Cf. A332218 (a subsequence).
%Y A332217 Cf. A000203, A007949, A013661, A332216.
%K A332217 nonn,changed
%O A332217 1,1
